        "original_id": "368146ad-8763-5c29-a330-cd810fcd5d57",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Stephen Frears, Christopher Hampton, John Malkovich, Glenn Close, Uma Thurman, Meryl Streep, Bryan Greenberg, Pierre Choderlos de Laclos\n- Films: Mary Reilly, Dangerous Liaisons, Prime\n- Works: Les liaisons dangereuses, Les Liaisons dangereuses\n- Topics: film adaptations, re-teaming, casting\n\nFacts:\n- In December 1985 and May 1986, Uma Thurman appeared on the covers of British Vogue.\n- Dangerous Liaisons is a 1988 American historical drama film.\n- Dangerous Liaisons was based on Christopher Hampton's play Les liaisons dangereuses, which adapted Pierre Choderlos de Laclos's 18th-century French novel Les Liaisons dangereuses.\n- In 1988, Uma Thurman starred in Dangerous Liaisons.\n- Mary Reilly re-teamed director Stephen Frears, screenwriter Christopher Hampton, and actors John Malkovich and Glenn Close, all of whom had worked on the Oscar-winning Dangerous Liaisons.\n- Prime is a 2005 American romantic comedy-drama film starring Uma Thurman, Meryl Streep, and Bryan Greenberg.",
